# native plans: filter, group by, sort and limit over FILE TABLE SCAN
Query Plan
=============================
|ID|OPERATOR           |NAME|
-----------------------------
|0 |TOP-N SORT         |    |
|1 |└─HASH GROUP BY    |    |
|2 |  └─FILE TABLE SCAN|o   |
=============================
Outputs & filters:
-------------------------------------
  0 - output([o.customer_id], [T_FUN_SUM(o.amount)]), filter(nil), rowset=16
      sort_keys([T_FUN_SUM(o.amount), DESC]), topn(2)
  1 - output([T_FUN_SUM(o.amount)], [o.customer_id]), filter(nil), rowset=16
      group([o.customer_id]), agg_func([T_FUN_SUM(o.amount)])
  2 - output([o.amount], [o.customer_id]), filter([o.amount > cast(10, DOUBLE(-1, -1))]), rowset=16
      access([o.amount], [o.customer_id]), read_csv('EXT_DIR/orders.csv')
Query Plan
===========================
|ID|OPERATOR         |NAME|
---------------------------
|0 |SCALAR GROUP BY  |    |
|1 |└─FILE TABLE SCAN|o   |
===========================
Outputs & filters:
-------------------------------------
  0 - output([T_FUN_COUNT(*)]), filter(nil), rowset=16
      group(nil), agg_func([T_FUN_COUNT(*)])
  1 - output(nil), filter(nil), rowset=16
